Key facts:
1. House style for multi-assertion: collect observations into one structure, single `expect(...).toEqual([...])`.
2. `check-spec-anchor-names.mjs` has a `--fix` mode that re-points the `#Lnn` from the test name it carries. Since there's no `reanchor.mjs`, this is the repo's tool for keeping links aligned — and it's a tiny node script (safe to run, it's not eslint). Running `node scripts/check-spec-anchor-names.mjs` (report) after my edits will verify the `#L40` still lands on the right test by name; `--fix` repairs it if it drifts.

